#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Long scrape registers: every named person and squad the indexes could not hold. No em-dashes."""
from page_lib import page, crumb, hero

page(
    "world/register.html",
    "Name register",
    "Every named Kagurabachi figure this archive can source through chapter 129, with doors into files.",
    crumb(("World", "index.html"), "Name register")
    + hero("Scrape · through Ironworks", "Name register", "人名録", "A directory, not a wiki dump. Names without a solo file live here until Jump gives them a room.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p>The character encyclopedia has solo files for Chihiro’s circle, the famous bearers, and the 2026 desks (Hokuto, Kuguri, Natsuki, Kasen, Subaru, Tafuku, Kiri, Ibuki). This register is everyone else the scrape could source, plus a one-line reminder of the people who already have pages. Two Hishaku and two wartime blades stay unlabeled. This archive will not invent them. Official chapters: VIZ / MANGA Plus.</p>

      <h2>Rokuhira house</h2>
      <p><a href="../characters/chihiro.html">Chihiro Rokuhira</a> (六平 千鉱). 18. 11 August. Enten. Taihi Kimura / Shoya Ishige. <a href="../characters/kunishige.html">Kunishige Rokuhira</a> (六平 国重). Seven blades. Tomokazu Seki / Kenta Fujimaki. <a href="../characters/chiaki.html">Chiaki Soga</a> (曽我 千晃). Mother. Princess Soga. Foresight. <a href="../characters/shiba.html">Togo Shiba</a> (柴 登吾). Teleport. Katsuyuki Konishi / Jun Fukushima. Hinao (ヒナオ). Cafe Haru Haru. Akari Tadano in the voiced comic. Connects sorcerers to yakuza and corporations who need them. The civilian door.</p>

      <h2>Enchanted Blade bearers</h2>
      <p><a href="../characters/akemura.html">Akemura Soga</a>, Magatsumi, Sword Master. <a href="../characters/samura.html">Seiichi Samura</a>, Tobimune. <a href="../characters/uruha.html">Yoji Uruha</a>, Kumeyuri. <a href="../characters/ibuki.html">Ibuki Misaka</a>, Cloud Gouger, dead. <a href="../characters/subaru.html">Subaru Urita</a> (瓜田 すば琉), unnamed blade, Sushi Subaru, Sand-Bone One-Sword Style, duplication, hachimaki, mustache, scar over the right eye, prolific smith before the war, helped Kunishige start the project, relocated after Sanso attacks. One war-ensemble portrait still unlabeled. Two wartime swords still unnamed. <a href="../characters/chihiro.html">Chihiro</a> holds Enten and held dying Cloud Gouger. <a href="../characters/iori.html">Iori</a> holds Tobimune after Samura. Hiruhiko held Kumeyuri until Ro recovered it. Kyora and Yura were Magatsumi proxies, not bearers.</p>

      <h2>Kamunabi leadership</h2>
      <p><a href="../characters/kasen.html">Kasen</a> (嘉仙), director, leak, barriers. Ichiki (壱鬼), elderly, small, trained Shiba and Azami, helped hide Kunishige, sealed Shinuchi. Yatsuru (夜弦), sole woman among named leaders, barriers and sealing, Shinuchi seal. <a href="../characters/azami.html">Soshiro Azami</a> (薊 奏士郎), Coin (Koin), strongest head, clinic art rewritten as execution. Izaru (亥猿), mutton chops, rosary bead chains, distrusts Chihiro, talks as if Kunishige stole the blades. Kudo (区堂), gas-mask apparatus, one eye closed, Warrior’s Path (Shitō), sends a body through walls, dies protecting Hakuri. White Robes: Kasen, Ichiki, Yatsuru. Full org: <a href="../factions/kamunabi.html">Kamunabi</a>.</p>

      <h2>Kamunabi operations</h2>
      <p><a href="../characters/hiyuki.html">Hiyuki Kagari</a>, Flame Bone of the Starving. <a href="../characters/tafuku.html">Tafuku Mihara</a> (美原 多福), duel domain, sumo silhouette, calm. <a href="../characters/natsuki.html">Natsuki Misaka</a> (巳坂奈ツ基), Lightning Menace (Raiku), squadron leader, Ibuki’s brother, Kumeyuri candidate, Volume 10 jacket. <a href="../characters/kiri.html">Kiri Shirakai</a> (白廻 斬), squadron leader, two-meter odachi, five-shaku blade, chapter 90, granddaughter of Itsuo, vow to decapitate him. Fushimi (伏見), Kokugoku Steam Squad, Smoke Axe (煙斧), cuts with smoke between hands, beats Datenseki troops, dies to Hiruhiko with the rest of the squad.</p>
      <p>Anti-Cloud Gouger Special Forces, six people, one sword, four graves. Ikuto Hagiwara (萩原 幾兎), commander, Jikai (磁戒), magnetism, loses both legs, later hallucinates Kugara, chapter 98’s cruel title, still useful in HQ. Hajime Kugara (具柄 一), iron body, mask, childhood friend of Hagiwara since age five, dies, the hallucination’s face. Kazane Machi (真智 カザネ), newest, Demon Monster (怪魑, Kaichi), the unused secret weapon, Sojo takes the right arm first. Shiyumi Harima (張間 梓弓), Gansui (岩垂), stone. Kiyohiko Uzuki (卯月 清彦), binding spells. Makoto Kasahara (笠原 誠), enlarged hands. Two survivors. That was the cavalry.</p>
      <p>Masumi (巻墨): Ro (郎), leader, over 23, child appearance, sunglasses and candy cigarettes copied off Samura, “get fired up,” recovers Kumeyuri, looks after Chihiro at Hakuri’s request. Moku (杢), tall, train station, feeds Chihiro when the boy starts eating himself, rallies Senkutsuji. Sumi (炭), cross tattoo on the right face, transportation mandalas drawn with a marker, motorcycle away from Kuguri, tends Hakuri so Storehouse can be used safely. They serve Samura, then are freed, then protect Iori in Operation: Easy Does It. Core Station Surveyor and operators, West Entrance Commander, Ishihira, Kashima: named as HQ furniture in tropes lists, not given rooms here.</p>

      <h2>Hishaku</h2>
      <p>Ten. Flame tattoos. Fire-gate. Eight printed. <a href="../characters/yura.html">Yura</a> (幽), leader. <a href="../characters/hokuto.html">Hokuto</a> (北兜), puppet armor, Ibuki’s killer. <a href="../characters/hiruhiko.html">Hiruhiko</a> (昼彦), Blood Crane, Play. <a href="../characters/kuguri.html">Kuguri</a> (久々李), Twilight Wave, unrequited blade. Toto (斗斗), blood tracking, fire-gate as habit, Iori job, Sengoku’s head as a sample. Uran (右嵐), ice, breath that freezes, raid on Kunishige. Bingo (瓶伍), Mako (魔咬), lion-dancer lucky charms, stacked weight on destroyers, eats corpses, gets sleepy. Yukisada (幸禎), 17, strongest fighter per Yura, regeneration past decapitation, Vessel in the HQ barrier. Two unnamed. Korogumi yakuza as allied muscle. Org: <a href="../factions/hishaku.html">Hishaku</a>.</p>

      <h2>Sazanami</h2>
      <p><a href="../characters/kyora.html">Kyora</a>, eleventh head. <a href="../characters/hakuri.html">Hakuri</a>, dual inheritance. Soya (漣 宗也), heir, obsessive, amnesia after the fall, volume extra about memories he wants gone. Tenri (漣 天理), short blades, Datenseki pop, jellyfish. Tamaki (漣 珠紀), older sister, lies to Kyora about Soya. Enji (漣 円慈), begs Shiba for death, is told to live. Org: <a href="../factions/sazanami.html">Sazanami</a>. Yuu Inazuma / Mr. Inazuma (稲妻 裕), child trying to break into the auction for his sister; Chihiro gets her out.</p>

      <h2>Soga and Mikaboshi</h2>
      <p>Chiaki, Akemura, already filed. Hiroto Soga (曽我 昼音), clan head, Kurotsuchi, directional gravity, levitate or crush, among the strongest before the war, killed on Irishima by Ariu. Yoshinojo Soga (曽我 義之丞), older, mustache and beard, cocky grin, unrelenting, killed by Ariu on the same island. Giyu Soga (曽我 義勇), Hiroto’s ambitious younger brother, next in line, willing to accept Mikaboshi demands that include handing Chiaki over. Ukizane Soga, historical, nearly destroyed the Mikaboshi before they hid under the sea. Ariu Mikaboshi (亜利雨 箕加星), crown prince, Sumika (栖), insect constructs, poisoned air, Datenseki-hardened body. The Mikaboshi king who built the undersea branch habitat is not given a modern name on this desk. Camp: Magatsumi copies Ariu. Not a caption.</p>

      <h2>Sorcery Bureau, still in Part 2</h2>
      <p>Shuji Mashiro (真城 秀治), Shiba’s partner, Akuu (空亜), air pressure, hands-free weapons, gifted a Kunishige sword at 18, opposes taking stolen Datenseki to the smith, dies later to Ariu, alive in the talks. Shinsaku Hasumi (蓮水 晋作), lab chief, comes to trust Kunishige, later resigns after letting Shiba steal ore, disillusioned when the bureau accepts Mikaboshi ceasefire terms. Joji (丈治), eyemask, nose ring, ranked above Shiba and Mashiro, annoyed. The Bureau becomes an army, then the Kamunabi. Part 2 is before that rename has finished meaning anything.</p>

      <h2>Other named</h2>
      <p><a href="../characters/char.html">Char Kyonagi</a> (鏡凪 シャル), last of the regenerative clan. Her mother, hunted with her, not given a separate file. Norisaku Madoka (円 法炸), Daruma sorcerer, Sojo’s employee, exploding Daruma, decides to go straight, killed by Sojo for talking. Chapter 8’s title is his name and a promise. Itsuo Shirakai (白廻逸夫), Iai founder, mountains, texts, bigot. Yojiro Sengoku (戦国与次郎), Kyoto Bloodshed Hotel, Reigen One-Sword Style, taught the staff, dies so Toto can read a head. Ikura (井倉), Iori’s classmate, loner, trails Toto, helps the seal break. The Shigyu brothers (死柳兄弟), hired chaos, eleven Kamunabi dead, Azami kills both. Goggles sorcerer on Natsuki’s Togo Squad: tropes name, no room. Pine-sorcery Hishaku hirelings at Senkutsuji: method, not names.</p>
      <p>Sojo (双城 厳一) already has the loudest file on the customer side. This register exists so the index stops pretending the war, the bureau, and the ten were four famous faces. <a href="../guide/cast.html">Who is who</a> is the short map. This is the long one. Techniques attached to these names: <a href="techniques.html">catalog</a>.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="../characters/index.html">Characters</a><a href="../guide/cast.html">Who is who</a><a href="../factions/index.html">Factions</a><a href="glossary.html">Glossary</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

page(
    "factions/masumi.html",
    "The Masumi",
    "Ro, Moku, and Sumi: the ninja clan that served Samura, erased Iori’s memories, and then chose the daughter over the myth.",
    crumb(("Factions", "index.html"), "Masumi")
    + hero("Ninja clan · Senkutsuji", "The Masumi", "巻墨", "Willing to die for a master until the master frees them. Then they work for the girl whose memories they stole.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p>The Masumi are a ninja clan loyal to the Kamunabi, known for a willingness to die for their master. After Kunishige’s death, three of them, Ro, Moku, and Sumi, guard <a href="../characters/samura.html">Seiichi Samura</a> at Senkutsuji Temple. When the Hishaku attack, they suppress sound and scent so a blind man can fight by hearing. They are prepared to die so he can leave. He refuses the sacrifice, rescues them, and later releases them from service. After his apparent betrayal, they join Chihiro for Operation: Easy Does It: protect <a href="../characters/iori.html">Iori</a>, the daughter whose memories of her father they themselves erased.</p>
      <p>That last clause is the clan’s whole moral. They are good at their job. The job included making a child forget a Buddhist swordsman so she could live through a war-crime backlash. The job later includes putting her on a motorcycle away from Kuguri. They do both. This page will not call that simple. It will call it the Masumi.</p>

      <h2>Ro</h2>
      <p>Leader. Over twenty-three. Looks like a child. Chihiro and Iori mistake him for one. He dislikes being treated as a kid and will still use the appearance to skip work. At Senkutsuji he takes on a Samura persona: sunglasses, candy cigarettes, “get fired up,” blunt manners. After the temple falls he visits Chihiro in hospital and says the Masumi will look out for him, per Hakuri’s request. He is the one who recovers Kumeyuri after Samura takes it off Hiruhiko at the hotel. A ninja clan’s leader doing inventory on a banquet sword is this book’s idea of logistics. He is not comic relief. He is what loyalty looks like when the master has sunglasses and a death wish.</p>

      <h2>Moku</h2>
      <p>Tall. Meets Hakuri and Uruha at the train station with Sumi. Rallies Senkutsuji’s troops when the Hishaku hit. Deeply empathetic in the way this book allows: when Chihiro starts doubting or chewing himself, Moku reminds him of the mission or shuts him up with food. The goldfish household’s manners, applied by a ninja. He is the clan’s gravity. Ro is the face. Sumi is the map. Moku is the reason Chihiro eats.</p>

      <h2>Sumi</h2>
      <p>Kunoichi. Cross-shaped tattoo on the right side of the face. Transportation mandalas, drawn with a marker: that is how Hakuri and Uruha reach Senkutsuji from the station. She tends Hakuri’s treatment so Storehouse can be used without killing him. In Operation: Easy Does It she takes Iori on a motorcycle while Kuguri gives chase. Blood tracking versus a drawn door. She is the reason the hotel is even a possible veil. Sengoku’s Reigen house is the building. Sumi’s marker is the road.</p>

      <h2>Operation: Easy Does It</h2>
      <p>Samura’s Owl is up. The Hishaku want Iori as a lever. The Masumi take her out of school toward Kyoto. Chihiro goes with them to tell her the truth rather than re-seal it. Kuguri and Toto hunt. The Kyoto Bloodshed Hotel is the chosen dark. Iori’s seal frays because she still loved her father and breaks when she shields Ikura. Hiruhiko wrecks the upper floors. Samura arrives. The Masumi do not get a volume jacket. They get the girl out of the myth long enough for her to choose a sword. After Samura dies, Tobimune is hers. The clan that erased him is still in the courtyard. That is not irony for its own sake. It is the job, finished as protection instead of erasure.</p>
      <p>They are Kamunabi-aligned and Samura-loyal and then Iori-loyal. The <a href="kamunabi.html">bureau page</a> lists them as Sanso-adjacent staff. This page lists them as people. Official chapters: VIZ / MANGA Plus.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="../characters/samura.html">Samura</a><a href="../characters/iori.html">Iori</a><a href="kamunabi.html">Kamunabi</a><a href="../arcs/sword-bearer.html">Sword Bearer Assassination</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

page(
    "factions/soga.html",
    "Soga and Mikaboshi",
    "Mainland prophecy aristocracy, old sorcerer kings under the sea, and the vein that brought them back to Irishima.",
    crumb(("Factions", "index.html"), "Soga and Mikaboshi")
    + hero("A thousand years, then a vein", "Soga and Mikaboshi", "曽我と箕加星", "Chiaki’s foresight is a warrant. Ariu’s insects are a camp. The island is a quarter-ton of rock with a royal family inside it.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p>The Soga were the most influential sorcerer clan in Japan for centuries before the Seitei War. A woman in each generation can see. That foresight is treated as inherited proof of Izanami, and it is why governments listen. Chiaki holds the Princess Soga title in Part 2. Akemura is her younger brother. They were elevated from a lower branch when the main-line prophetess died without children. The clan is not a single will. Hiroto is the stoic head. Yoshinojo is the grinning veteran. Giyu is the ambitious brother who might trade the princess. Shiba guarded them. Kunishige sold swords to people he could stand, which included this house, which is how a picky civilian becomes the man who will smelt their war.</p>
      <p>The Mikaboshi were sorcerer kings. The Soga pushed them off the mainland more than a thousand years ago. Ukizane Soga nearly finished them. The Mikaboshi king used Datenseki to build an enormous spherical habitat of branches under the ocean. They adapted. When Irishima’s earthquake showed a vein and Shokoku rose from the sea, they came back for the ore. The Seitei War is that return. Ariu, crown prince, kills Hiroto and Yoshinojo on the island. The blades enter at plus one year and five months. Shokoku overthrows its royals and signs a peace. Akemura voids the peace with flowers. About 200,000 civilians. The Kamunabi file it as heroes. Part 2 is the talks before that filing.</p>

      <h2>The Soga in the present tense of Part 2</h2>
      <p>Chiaki: foresight, title, Kunishige’s hope in chapter 129’s fire, Chihiro’s mother, not yet. Akemura: not yet Sword Master, still the friend a smith trusts, still the brother a princess loves. Hiroto: Kurotsuchi, directional gravity, crush or levitate, among the strongest alive before Datenseki royalty walks onto Irishima. Yoshinojo: experienced, eager, dies with Hiroto to Ariu. Giyu: next in line, willing to accept ceasefire terms that include handing Chiaki over. That last fact is why a title is also a hostage tag. Shiba tells Kunishige not to lose hope when the princess rank puts distance between them. The clan’s warrant is Chiaki’s eyes. The clan’s risk is everyone who wants those eyes in a different building.</p>

      <h2>Ariu and the camp</h2>
      <p>Ariu Mikaboshi: Sumika, insect constructs, poisoned air that dulls senses, a body Datenseki has already rewritten. After chapter 119, explainers argued Magatsumi is those insects recast in Kunishige’s steel: wartime blades as six royal sorcerers copied. Useful camp. Not a caption this page will print as fact. What is printed: once Magatsumi entered the field, Japan could walk onto the island. What is printed: Magatsumi has no three-count and overwrites other bodies. What is printed: Malediction. The camp sits next to the <a href="../world/techniques.html">insect kit</a>. When Jump makes it cheap to source, the camp becomes a sentence. Until then, Ariu is the prince who kills two Soga on Irishima and poisons the air around a war for a vein.</p>

      <h2>Why this is the setting</h2>
      <p>The Kamunabi exist because this war existed. Enchanted Blades exist because Shiba believed Kunishige’s eyes could turn the vein into something other than craters. Enten exists because the wartime six could not be smashed after Akemura used one of them as policy. Chihiro’s revenge exists because Kasen leaked a smith who was sorry. Part 2 exists because the book is willing to put a conference table and a kiln on the page instead of another hotel. The Soga are the mainland’s warning system. The Mikaboshi are the warning, coming back. Datenseki is the object. Flowers are what a trusted friend does with the object after a treaty. See <a href="../analysis/irishima.html">Irishima’s vein</a>, <a href="../manga/part-2.html">the forge desk</a>, <a href="../characters/chiaki.html">Chiaki</a>, <a href="../characters/akemura.html">Akemura</a>, <a href="../analysis/malediction.html">Malediction</a>.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="index.html">Factions</a><a href="../world/index.html">Timeline</a><a href="../arcs/seitei-war.html">Seitei War</a><a href="../analysis/irishima.html">Vein essay</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

page(
    "world/sanso.html",
    "Sanso fortresses",
    "Kamunabi strongholds that locked surviving Enchanted Blade bearers after the Rokuhira raid, and the attacks that opened Part 1’s long book.",
    crumb(("World", "index.html"), "Sanso")
    + hero("Bearer vaults", "Sanso", "山荘", "After Hokuto opened Cloud Gouger, the bureau put the rest of the war in buildings. The Hishaku spent three years trying to open the buildings.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p>Sanso are Kamunabi fortresses assigned to surviving wartime Enchanted Blade bearers after the Rokuhira raid and Ibuki’s murder. The logic is the Lifelong Contract: while the bearer lives, the Hishaku cannot fully sign the stolen steel. Lock the person, stall the ten. It works until it does not. Kokugoku is attacked. Senkutsuji is attacked. Subaru is relocated. The long book of Part 1, Sword Bearer Assassination, is the Sanso system meeting a method that had three years of practice. This page is the buildings. The <a href="../factions/kamunabi.html">Kamunabi page</a> is the bureau that staffed them. The <a href="../factions/hishaku.html">Hishaku page</a> is the method.</p>

      <h2>Kokugoku Hot Spring</h2>
      <p>Uruha’s Sanso. The Kokugoku Steam Squad, including Fushimi and Smoke Axe, are the guard. Hishaku-hired Datenseki troops hit first. The squad beats them. Then Hiruhiko arrives. Blood Crane, mercenary sorcerers, a train, a kabuki house. The Steam Squad dies. Chihiro fights Hiruhiko so Hakuri can move Uruha toward Senkutsuji. Chapter 48 is titled for the squad. They get a name and a grave in the same week. That is how the bureau spends specialists: named, competent, insufficient. The Anti-Cloud Gouger Special Forces were the same sentence in the first book.</p>

      <h2>Senkutsuji Temple</h2>
      <p>Samura’s Sanso, in the sense that a blind Buddhist swordsman and three Masumi are the Kamunabi’s idea of a vault. Pine-sorcery hirelings attack. The Masumi suppress sound and scent. Hakuri delivers Tobimune through Storehouse. Samura clears the temple. Then he cuts Uruha down. Suzaku: kill the contract, keep the man. The Hishaku think they have a partner who will eliminate bearers. He is lying about the dying. Owl goes up nationwide. The temple is no longer a Sanso. It is a launch site for a detection technique and a betrayal that is also a rescue. Ro, Moku, and Sumi leave with a different job: Iori.</p>

      <h2>The ones not on the page yet</h2>
      <p>Subaru Urita is moved rather than used as bait. Duplication sorcery makes a contract-opening assassination a poor match; kill one Subaru, another still holds the unnamed blade. Akemura is not in a Sanso. He is in a cell under HQ, which is a fortress of a different kind, the kind a director can leak around and a Vessel can split. Magatsumi’s master key is why that cell exists: if Akemura dies, the other wartime bearers die. Sanso without the basement is incomplete logistics. The basement without Sanso is a myth. Kasen wanted the steel. The buildings were the compromise until he sold the smith.</p>
      <p>Chihiro’s deal after the Rakuzaichi (Hakuri as logistics, Magatsumi to the state, Enten in his hand) assumes Sanso can be used as a circuit rather than a prison: touch a bearer, Storehouse the blade, do not siege the mountain. The Hishaku assault on a fortress is what makes the table deploy that circuit in a hurry. The next book starts on a train because a building failed. Locations desk: <a href="locations.html">locations</a>. Arc: <a href="../arcs/sword-bearer.html">Sword Bearer Assassination</a>. Surviving unnamed bearer: <a href="../characters/subaru.html">Subaru</a>.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="../factions/kamunabi.html">Kamunabi</a><a href="../factions/masumi.html">Masumi</a><a href="../characters/uruha.html">Uruha</a><a href="../world/contracts.html">Contracts</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

print("long pages done")
